      "id": "objets",
      "title": "Vocabulaire des objets",
      "minutes": 5,
      "lede": "Un / une — pratiquez le genre de chaque objet.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Every noun has a gender",
          "text": "Every French noun is masculine (un / le) or feminine (une / la), and the gender is usually arbitrary. Learn each noun together with its article: un livre, une chaise.\n- Rough hints: -tion, -té and -ure are usually feminine; -age, -ment and -eur are usually masculine. Exceptions: une image, une page, une plage, une fleur.\n- Before a vowel, le and la both become l' (l'horloge), so the gender becomes invisible. Remember it is une horloge.\n- The plural article is des for both genders: des livres, des chaises."
        },
